{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# DC one-way segmenting wiki renderer (behind the WikiTextCodec seam)\n\n## Context / Problem\nJira Data Center stores rich text as wiki markup (REST v2), a lossy text format.\nThe `RichTextCodec` seam (epic `e369`, story J3 / `aac8-…`) already routes DC\nrich text through **`WikiTextCodec`** (`adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py`),\ntoday an **identity** codec: `to_wire`/`normalize_outbound`/`decode_inbound` all\npass the plain string through unchanged. So DC currently ships rebar's raw\nMarkdown as literal wiki source.\n\nNo library round-trips rebar's punctuation-dense prose: pandoc's jira reader\nmisparses `->`, ASCII pipe-tables, and regex, and provably erodes them one\ncharacter per pass (the ASCII-table body decays 9115→9110 monotonically). A\nwhole-body all-or-nothing conversion is echo-safe but only ~15% rich. A\n**segmenting** one-way renderer that converts only structurally-safe units and\npasses dangerous ones through verbatim reaches ~68% of bodies / ~78% of chars\nrich, proven non-corrupting across 23 environments, 6 authors, and an\nout-of-distribution corpus.\n\nThis story replaces `WikiTextCodec`'s identity outbound with a segmenting\nMD→wiki renderer, **one-way** (echo-safety comes from the separate\nstate-suppression story `3388-…`, so this codec does NOT need to be a fixed\npoint).\n\n## Prior art in this repo (the seam we build on — NOT greenfield)\n- `WikiTextCodec` (DC) — `adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py:72`, currently\n  identity. Constructed into the shared `OutboundFieldMapper` at\n  `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:84`.\n- `RichTextCodec` Protocol — `adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py`; four ops. The\n  wire-shape op is `to_wire` (DC: a wiki `str`); the intended composition is\n  `to_wire(normalize_outbound(fit_outbound(text)))` (proven in\n  `test_rich_text_codec.py:53`). **`to_wire` is defined and unit-tested but not\n  yet consumed by the live DC send** — connecting it is part of this work.\n- DC outbound send — `OutboundFieldMapper.map_fields_to_remote`\n  (`adapters/jira_family/outbound_mapper.py:41`) builds `out[\"description\"]`,\n  which reaches `transport.py:265 update_issue` → `issue.update(fields=…)`\n  (`transport.py:287`). This is the DC analog of Cloud's ADF encode at\n  `adapters/jira/acli.py:205` (`_text_to_adf`).\n- **Guard:** `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:131 normalize_rich_text` is the\n  **INBOUND** decode and delegates to the SHARED plain-text\n  `inbound_fields.normalize_rich_text` (ticket 21ca) — it is NOT the outbound\n  render seam and is left unchanged. (The original plan mis-targeted it.)\n- **Import contract (ADR 0035):** `jira_family/` must not import\n  `adapters/jira/`. pandoc/`pypandoc` is not a Cloud module, so the renderer may\n  live in `jira_family/` (or `jira_datacenter/`) and call it.\n\n## Approach\nImplement the segmenting renderer as **`WikiTextCodec.to_wire`** (delegating to a\nnew renderer module to respect the module-size cap) and **wire `to_wire` into the\nDC outbound send** so `update_issue` receives rendered wiki — mirroring the Cloud\n`_text_to_adf` encode boundary. Leave `normalize_outbound`/`fit_outbound` and the\ninbound `normalize_rich_text` unchanged.\n\nPipeline: split the body into blocks and list-items; render structurally-safe\nunits (headings, lists, code, quotes, safe paragraphs) to wiki via pinned\n`pandoc` (`-f commonmark -t jira --wrap=none`); pass dangerous units (ASCII\ntables, arrow/regex/HTML-dense prose) through **verbatim**; reassemble in\noriginal order. Two lossless render rules: **code-aware arrow substitution**\n(`-> <- <-> =>` → `→ ← ↔ ⇒`, prose-only, skipping fenced/inline code) which MUST\nrun on the **Markdown before pandoc** (after pandoc, code is `{{…}}` and prose\n`->` is already escaped, so a post-render pass misfires); and **verbatim-wrapping\nASCII tables in `{noformat}`** to stop the per-pass dash erosion. Ship\n**descriptions before comments** (descriptions convert 100% some-rich / 30% chars\nvs comments 63% / 23.6%).\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py` —\n  `WikiTextCodec.to_wire` delegates to the new renderer.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py` (new) —\n  segmenting renderer (split → per-unit safe-render/passthrough → reassemble;\n  arrow substitution; table wrap). Lives in `jira_family/` (ADR-0035-clean).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/` — apply\n  `codec.to_wire` to the description on the DC outbound send (the encode boundary).\n- `pyproject.toml` — pinned `pypandoc` extra.\n- **Guard:** `jira_datacenter/backend.py:131 normalize_rich_text` (inbound,\n  shared) is NOT changed.\n- `tests/` — segmenting/arrow/table corpus tests.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy path: a description of headings + a checklist + a fenced code block\n  renders to wiki `h1.`/`*`-bullets/`{code}` via `to_wire` and reassembles in\n  original order.\n- Danger passthrough: a body with an ASCII pipe-table, a prose `->`, and a\n  `obj->method()` code arrow renders with the table verbatim in `{noformat}`,\n  prose `->`→`→`, and the code arrow untouched.\n- Send wiring: a DC outbound description update calls `to_wire` so\n  `issue.update(fields=…)` receives rendered wiki, not raw Markdown; verified by\n  `test_dc_outbound_renders_wiki` asserting the transport payload.\n- Corpus coverage/safety: over the historical corpus the renderer yields rich for\n  ~68% of bodies with 0 code-arrow rewrites and 0 prose corruptions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `WikiTextCodec.to_wire` segments a body and renders only structurally-safe\n  units, passing dangerous units (tables/arrows/regex/HTML) verbatim; verified by\n  `test_dc_segmenting_passthrough` on a mixed body.\n- [ ] The DC outbound send applies `to_wire` so the description reaching\n  `update_issue` is rendered wiki (not raw Markdown), while the inbound\n  `normalize_rich_text` stays plain-text; verified by `test_dc_outbound_renders_wiki`\n  and the existing inbound tests staying green.\n- [ ] Code-aware arrow substitution runs on the Markdown before pandoc and touches\n  0 code arrows; verified by a test asserting `obj->method()` is unchanged while a\n  prose `->` becomes `→` (regression over the 179 known code-arrow bodies: 0\n  rewrites).\n- [ ] ASCII tables are verbatim-wrapped in `{noformat}` and do not erode across\n  passes; verified by `test_dc_table_noformat_stable` over the known erosion\n  bodies (70/70 stable).\n- [ ] Over the historical corpus the renderer produces rich output for ≈68% of\n  bodies / ≈78% of chars with zero prose corruption; verified by\n  `test_dc_corpus_coverage`."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785804787902030001,"uuid":"de1e8f80-7d48-4bb8-b676-824fcbe62818"}